 "coaching_points": [
  "Warm up first \u2014 2-3 min light jogging, open-hip and lateral shuffles, a few easy side-to-side touches",
  "How it works \u2014 attacker starts with the ball and attacks either gate; defender wins if they steal it clean, force a bad touch, or delay the attack 3+ seconds without lunging",
  "Do NOT dive in \u2014 approach fast, brake early, arrive on the balls of your feet in a low staggered stance",
  "Read the attacker's hips and the ball, not the shoulders \u2014 commit only when the touch is too far from their foot",
  "Show them ONE gate \u2014 angle your body to force them onto their weaker foot toward the gate you choose to defend",
  "Jockey and shepherd: stay half a body-width goal-side, match their pace, deny the straight line and wait for the mistake",
  "6 attacks per set, then swap roles; 4 sets \u2014 the walk back between reps is your rest",
  "Target \u2014 defender delays or wins the ball in 4 of every 6 attacks without fouling",
  "Progression: attacker gets a 2-touch limit to speed up decisions; regression: widen the gap to give the defender more recovery time"
 ],
 "variations": [
  "One gate only \u2014 defender commits fully to forcing the attacker away from a single target",
  "Time-attack \u2014 attacker must beat the defender within 4 seconds or the defender wins the rep"
 ],
